At least it's only on shutdown, though figuring out why would still be interesting.

Here's the code:
https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/6644d3feaba30ccd649662f5863cdc531d222dc5/src/libraries/System.IO.Pipelines/src/System/IO/Pipelines/StreamPipeReader.cs#L526-L530
```
        private ReadOnlySequence<byte> GetCurrentReadOnlySequence()
        {
            Debug.Assert(_readHead != null && _readTail != null);
            return new ReadOnlySequence<byte>(_readHead, _readIndex, _readTail, _readTail.End);
        }
```

The only statement that could null ref is `_readTail.End`, and there's even a `Debug.Assert` that `_readTail` shouldn't be null.

The call stack seems to point here:
https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/6644d3feaba30ccd649662f5863cdc531d222dc5/src/libraries/System.IO.Pipelines/src/System/IO/Pipelines/StreamPipeReader.cs#L266

